# What claude-test.sh runs: one Claude session per layout (reachable, top), each with its cases, and each session's bounds.
# A case runs in both layouts only when the layouts render it differently; the rest run in one.
# entries-<layout> (optional) tells that session which directory entries and names its cases use, so none meets an entry already known.
model: claude-haiku-5-5
layouts: reachable top
cases-reachable: C1-C9, D1-D15, U1-U3, W1-W11 and G1-G4 (no names setup: the N cases and the full search run in another session)
cases-top: C1-C4 (this layout places the tags and the search rows differently), D1, D2, D4, D7 and D8 (the header, the page order and "Show more" in this layout's list) and D15 (the onboarding pages swap with the results); the rest look the same in both layouts
entries-reachable: D6 joins the channel ci_channel (search "ci seed"), which U1 and U2 then use; W6 opens the channel ci_avatar_c1 from New chat (search "ci avatar"); D14 and D15 use a second profile you add, which has no conversations; ci_cards, which the smoke test joined, is for no case
entries-top: the earlier session joined ci_channel and may have opened ci_avatar_c1 and added a second profile; the top-bar cases join nothing
max-turns: 900
max-budget-usd: 5
